## Lore

Rulian Translators are in high demand at the Splynn Dimensional Market. Even god-like beings do not know every language; magical speech unnerves some listeners and does not last, psionic communication carries a similar stigma, and mechanical translators are limited, slow and inaccurate. Having a Rulian translator is fashionable in Atlantis and the Three Galaxies, and one is a common member of any powerful being''s entourage.

Rulians are natural telepathic and empathic receivers with an unmatched talent for understanding, translating and learning languages. Strong, flexible vocal cords give them a huge range of sounds, from super-low vibrations to ultrasonics, and their gift for language makes them masters of linguistics, mathematics and decryption. Beneath a cold, alien exterior lies the heart of a poet; enslaved, these deeply emotional people feel the cruelty around them, and many are driven to suicide. Set free, most become travelers who turn their experiences into poems, verse and song, more fantastic than factual.

## Body

A bit shorter than humans at the shoulder, but an extended cranium adds a foot of height: 6 to 7 feet (1.8 to 2.1 m) tall, 150 to 180 lbs (67.5 to 81 kg). They can live 100 years, but most die much earlier (20-35), by their own hand or a cruel master''s. NPCs are level 1D6+1.

## GM Notes

Habitat: their homeworld is very earth-like, so they can live in all but the most hostile places on Earth. Value: 100,000-150,000 credits on average, rising with their popularity. Allies: none as such, but most enjoy the company of like-minded, educated humanoids. Enemies: the Splugorth, their minions and all evil enslavers. Phase World: a fairly large population of free and enslaved Rulians lives in the Three Galaxies, where they know all six Trade Languages and two others at 98% in place of the beginning languages, and are vital to an economy of over a million races.
